# Claude Code Project Rules - Imaginary Builder AI

## Documentation Reference
Always follow the patterns and guidelines documented in the `/docs` folder.
Full documentation index: `/docs/README.md`

## Architecture Patterns

### Queries Layer (CRITICAL)
- **ALL React Query hooks MUST be in `src/queries/`** - organized by domain
- Never define useQuery/useMutation in components or hooks/ folder
- One file per domain matching service organization (e.g., orderQueries.ts, productQueries.ts)
- Use consistent query keys: `["domain", id]` or `["domain", { filters }]`
- Always invalidate caches in mutations

### Component Organization
- **Feature-based organization** - group by feature/domain, NOT by type
- ❌ Bad: `components/buttons/`, `components/inputs/`
- ✅ Good: `components/checkout/`, `components/dashboard/`
- Co-locate related files (component, styles, tests) in same folder
- Place truly shared components in `components/common/`

### File Organization
- **NO barrel exports (index.ts)** - use direct imports from file paths
- ❌ Bad: `import { Button } from '@/features/ui'`
- ✅ Good: `import { Button } from '@/features/ui/button'`
- Exception: Only if 2+ files are ALWAYS imported together

### Layer Separation
```
Components → Queries (React Query) → Services (Business Logic) → API/Database
```

## Design System & Styling

### Component Priority
1. **First**: Use shadcn/ui components from `@/features/ui/`
2. **Second**: Extend shadcn with className prop
3. **Last resort**: Create custom components only when shadcn doesn't provide functionality

### Styling Standards
- **Always use `clsx`** for conditional styling (never template literals)
- Use theme components from `@/theme/components` for reusable styles
- Only add to theme if used in 2+ components
- Define static style constants OUTSIDE components
- Use Next.js `Image` component instead of `<img>` tags
- Use icon components from `@/theme/icons` instead of inline SVGs

### Semantic HTML
- Always use semantic elements: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`
- Never use generic `<div>` where semantic elements apply
- One `<main>` per page

## Accessibility (MANDATORY)

### WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance Required
- Minimum color contrast: 4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for large text
- All interactive elements keyboard accessible
- Proper ARIA attributes (aria-label, aria-describedby, aria-invalid)
- Visible focus indicators (focus:ring-2 patterns)
- Touch targets minimum 44px on mobile
- Screen reader support with semantic HTML

### Required Attributes
- `htmlFor` linking labels to inputs
- `aria-label` for elements without visible text
- `role="alert"` for error messages
- `aria-live` for dynamic content

## TypeScript Standards

### Naming Conventions
- **Interfaces**: End with `I` (e.g., `UserI`, `OrderI`)
- **Types**: End with `T` (e.g., `StatusT`, `ErrorCodeT`)
- **Component Props**: Use `Props` for single-component, descriptive name if shared
- **Hooks**: Prefix with `use` (e.g., `useOrderFilters`)

### Usage
- Interfaces for object shapes, props, API entities
- Types for unions, computed types, utility types
- Zod schemas for runtime validation with `z.infer<typeof Schema>`

## React Patterns

### Client Components
- Only use `"use client"` when necessary (state, effects, events, browser APIs)
- Don't use for static/presentational components

### Hooks Organization
- React Query hooks → `src/queries/` (ALL queries/mutations)
- Component-specific non-query hooks → same folder as component
- Shared utility hooks → `src/hooks/`

### Ref Handling
- **Avoid forwardRef and useImperativeHandle** - prefer callback patterns
- Use trigger props instead of imperative APIs
- Only acceptable for low-level DOM element exposure

### State Management
- React Query for server state
- Zustand for global client state
- React Context with `use-context-selector` for feature-scoped state
- Use selector hooks to prevent unnecessary re-renders

## Error Handling (MANDATORY)

### Service Layer
- **ALL service methods MUST wrap fetch in try-catch**
- Handle network errors, HTTP errors, parsing errors
- Provide contextual error messages
- Re-throw with additional context

### Component Layer
- Use `useErrorHandler` hook for consistent error handling
- Show user-friendly messages with error codes
- Always handle loading and error states for data fetching
- Create shimmer loading components (separate file)

## Testing Requirements (MANDATORY)

### End-to-End Tests
- **Every new user action MUST have E2E tests**
- Co-locate test files with components (`Component.e2e.spec.ts`)
- Test success paths AND failure scenarios
- Test edge cases, validation, API failures, error recovery

### Checklist for New Features
- [ ] Success path works
- [ ] Form validation with errors
- [ ] API failure handling
- [ ] Loading states display
- [ ] Edge cases tested
- [ ] Error recovery works
- [ ] Accessibility verified
- [ ] Responsive design works

## Code Quality

### Best Practices
- Remove unused imports immediately
- No "use client" unless necessary
- Use Next.js Link component for navigation (not router.push)
- Comprehensive error handling in all async operations
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks
- Form validation with React Hook Form + Zod

### Navigation
- Use `<Button asChild><Link href="/path">Text</Link></Button>`
- Never `<Button onClick={() => router.push("/path")}>`

## Development Workflow

### Commands
- `npm run dev` - Development server
- `npm run build` - Production build
- `npm run supabase:types` - Generate DB types after schema changes
- `npm run lint` - ESLint check

### When Adding Features
1. Check if queries layer hooks exist, create in `src/queries/` if needed
2. Use shadcn/ui components first
3. Follow feature-based organization
4. Add E2E tests in same folder
5. Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
6. Handle loading/error states
7. Use semantic HTML
8. Remove unused imports

## Critical Rules Summary
✅ DO:
- All queries in src/queries/
- Feature-based organization
- shadcn/ui components first
- clsx for conditional styles
- Semantic HTML
- WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
- E2E tests for new features
- Comprehensive error handling
- Direct imports (no index.ts)

❌ DON'T:
- useQuery/useMutation in components
- Type-based organization
- Barrel exports (index.ts)
- Template literals for conditional styles
- Generic <div> where semantic elements apply
- Skip accessibility requirements
- Skip error handling
- Create custom components when shadcn exists
